# Vue coding style

Narrows `core-common-rules`' style rules to Vue Single File Component
conventions. Applies only to `*.vue`; the `<script>` block's TypeScript style
comes from `ts-js-node`'s coding-style rule.

## Script setup and typing

- Use `<script setup lang="ts">` for new components; no Options API or bare `<script>` in new files unless the project has no `<script setup>` components yet.
- Declare props type-only, `defineProps<{ ... }>()`, not the runtime-object form; use `withDefaults(defineProps<Props>(), { ... })` for defaults, not mutation of the props object.
- Declare emits type-only with named-tuple syntax, `defineEmits<{ change: [id: number] }>()`, not the string-array form.
- Vue 3.5+: destructure `defineProps()` directly (`const { title } = defineProps<Props>()`). Pre-3.5: keep the props object intact (`props.title`, or `toRefs(props)`).
- Type `ref<T>()` explicitly when the initial value infers narrower than the eventual type (`ref<string | null>(null)`).

## Naming and structure

- `PascalCase` component file and `name` (`OrderSummary.vue`); composables `camelCase` prefixed `use` (`useOrderTotals.ts`).
- One component per `.vue` file; markup repeated within a template becomes a child component, not a `v-for` over inline duplicates.
- Order SFC blocks `<script setup>`, `<template>`, `<style>` (or the project's established order); no third ordering.
- Multi-word component names (`UserCard`, not `Card`), per `eslint-plugin-vue`'s `multi-word-component-names`.

## Formatting and imports

- Format with the project's configured formatter; do not hand-format around it.
- Run the project's `eslint` with `eslint-plugin-vue`; fix what it flags, no blanket disable comment.
- Use auto-imported composables/components only when `unplugin-auto-import`/`unplugin-vue-components` (or Nuxt) is configured; otherwise import explicitly.

## Errors

- Surface a composable or store action's failure to the caller (thrown error or a returned error/result shape), not a bare `catch` with no rethrow and no user-visible state change.
- Use `onErrorCaptured` (component-tree scope) or `app.config.errorHandler` (app-wide) for error boundaries, not ad hoc `try/catch` around every template-triggered call.
